docs\reviews\20260812-0045-slice-platform.md:15:  `acquire_lock` writes its own `os.getpid()` (tools/preflight.py:124), but in the n8n path (n8n/novel_workflow.json runs `python tools/preflight.py --db demo.db` at start and `tools/release_lock.py` at the end) that process exits right after acquiring. The stale check (lines 139-147) then treats any lock whose PID is dead as stale — reproduced: a 10-second-old lock with a dead PID is unlinked and re-acquired — so a second run starting while the first run is still in progress steals the lock, both pass preflight, and both can publish (the double-publish the lock exists to prevent). The docstring's "lock younger than 2h is considered held regardless of PID" contradicts the code, which only applies the 2h rule when the PID cannot be parsed. editorial_daily.py's in-process use is unaffected; the n8n path is vulnerable.
